*Testing** \u2013 QA began regression testing on Module A and reported no critical blockers.\n4. **Risks & Mitigations** \u2013 Identified a potential delay in third\u2011party API integration; we\u2019ve scheduled a call with the vendor for Thursday to resolve the issue.\n5. **Next Steps** \u2013 Focus on completing the remaining development tasks, start performance testing, and prepare the demo for the stakeholder review meeting on Friday.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or need further details.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\nProject Lead"}, "outputs": {"status": "drafted", "to": ["team@example.com"], "subject": "Weekly Project Status Update"}, "session_index": 3, "session_type": "trigger"}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-23 10:11:40.778343+00:00", "tool_name": "EmailTool", "operation": "send_email", "inputs": {"to": ["team@example.com"], "subject": "Weekly Project Status Update", "body": "Hi Team,\n\nHere\u2019s a brief summary of this week\u2019s progress:\n\n1. **Milestone 1 Completed** \u2013 The initial design specifications have been finalized and approved.\n2. **Development Sprint** \u2013 Completed 80% of the planned user\u2011story tickets; remaining items are on track for next week.\n3. **Testing** \u2013 QA began regression testing on Module A and reported no critical blockers.\n4. **Risks & Mitigations** \u2013 Identified a potential delay in third\u2011party API integration; we\u2019ve scheduled a call with the vendor for Thursday to resolve the issue.\n5. **Next Steps** \u2013 Focus on completing the remaining development tasks, start performance testing, and prepare the demo for the stakeholder review meeting on Friday.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or need further details.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\nProject Lead"}, "outputs": {"status": "sent", "to": ["team@example.com"], "subject": "Weekly Project Status Update"}, "session_index": 3, "session_type": "trigger"}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-23 10:11:35.410949+00:00", "tool_n