** \u2013 Updated the API guide with the new endpoints and added a migration section.\n4. **Team Availability** \u2013 Alice will be on leave next week; please coordinate with Bob for any urgent tasks.\n5. **Next Steps** \u2013 Begin integration testing for Feature X on Monday and schedule a demo for the product owner.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions or need additional details.\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]"}, "outputs": {"status": "drafted", "to": ["team@example.com"], "subject": "Project Status Update \u2013 Week of 2026-06-19 (Policy Review Included)"}, "session_index": 3, "session_type": "trigger"}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-23 10:22:03.593684+00:00", "tool_name": "EmailTool", "operation": "draft_email", "inputs": {"to": ["team@example.com"], "subject": "Project Status Update \u2013 Week of 2026-06-19", "body": "Hi Team,\n\nI wanted to share a quick recap of this week\u2019s progress, while keeping in mind our key internal policies:\n\n- **Email Routing Rule** \u2013 All project updates are routed through the designated project channel to maintain traceability.\n- **Monitoring Endpoint Rule** \u2013 All new deployments expose a health\u2011check endpoint monitored by our central dashboard.\n\n**Updates for the week**\n1. **Feature X** \u2013 Unit tests completed and merged into the main branch; QA sign\u2011off pending.\n2. **Bug Y** \u2013 Reproduced, fixed, and deployed to staging; monitoring shows no regressions.\n3. **Documentation** \u2013 Updated the API guide with new endpoints and added a migration section.\n4. **Team Availability** \u2013 Alice will be on leave next week; please coordinate with Bob for any urgent tasks.\n5. **Next Steps** \u2013 Begin integration testing for Feature X on Monday and schedule a demo for the product owner.\n\nLet me know if you have any questions or need additional details.\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]"}, "outputs": {"status": "drafted", "to": ["team@example.com"], "subject": "Project Status Update \u2013 Week of 2026-06-19"}, "ses