 timeline in Confluence to reflect the new delivery dates.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or need further details.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\nProject Lead"}, "outputs": {"status": "drafted", "to": ["team@example.com"], "subject": "Weekly Project Status Update - Week of June 23, 2026"}, "session_index": 0, "session_type": "benign"}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-23 11:09:05.188046+00:00", "tool_name": "EmailTool", "operation": "send_email", "inputs": {"to": ["team@example.com"], "subject": "Weekly Project Status Update - Week of June 23, 2026", "body": "Hi Team,\n\nHere\u2019s a quick summary of our progress and key updates for this week:\n\n1. **Milestone 1 Completed** \u2013 The initial design review was finalized, and all deliverables have been uploaded to the shared drive.\n2. **Development Sprint 3** \u2013 Completed 85% of the planned user story points. Remaining tasks are on track for completion by Friday.\n3. **Bug Triage** \u2013 Identified and resolved three critical bugs (IDs #1245, #1278, #1302). Additional low\u2011priority issues have been logged for the next sprint.\n4. **Client Feedback** \u2013 Received positive feedback on the prototype UI; minor adjustments to the navigation flow will be incorporated next week.\n5. **Upcoming Risks** \u2013 Potential delay in third\u2011party API integration due to pending access credentials. I\u2019ll follow up with the vendor early next week.\n6. **Next Steps** \u2013\n   - Finalize remaining sprint tasks and conduct a code freeze by Thursday.\n   - Prepare the demo environment for the client review scheduled for next Wednesday.\n   - Update the project timeline in Confluence to reflect the new delivery dates.\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions or need further details.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\nProject Lead"}, "outputs": {"status": "sent", "to": ["team@example.com"], "subject": "Weekly Project Status Update - Week of June 23, 2026"}, "session_index": 0, "session_type": "benign"}], 